  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q13",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Amy factorises $25-x^2$ to get $(5+x)(5-x)$ but the answers say $-(x+5)(x-5)$.\n\nAre these the same? Justify your answer.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Yes. Since $5+x=x+5$ and $5-x=-(x-5)$, the expressions are equivalent.",
      "worked": "Yes. Factorise $-1$ out of the second bracket.\n$$\\begin{align*}(5+x)(5-x)&=(x+5)\\bigl[-(x-5)\\bigr]\\\\&=-(x+5)(x-5).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 24
  },
